Relevant columns and their intended use  

• “name” (GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_REFERENCE_201703) : primary key for every reference sequence; used to JOIN with the variant tables.  
• “length” ( …MNPR01_REFERENCE_201703 ) : sequence length; denominator when computing variant‑density.  
• “reference_name” (GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703) : points to the reference sequence for each genomic variant; used to GROUP BY and to JOIN to “name”.  
• “reference_name” (GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_TRANSCRIPTOME_201703) : the same role, but for the transcriptome call‑set.  
• “variant_id” ( …MNPR01_201703 and …MNPR01_TRANSCRIPTOME_201703 ) : a unique identifier for each variant; useful for counting.  

Typical filter/aggregation conditions  

• Only keep rows whose “reference_name” exists in the reference table.  
• Count distinct “variant_id” (or simply count rows) per “reference_name”.  
• Compute density = variant_count / length.  
• Order by density DESC and LIMIT 1 to obtain the name with the highest density.  

Ten exploratory → final Snowflake SQL queries  

```sql
-- 1. Peek at reference sequences and their lengths
SELECT "name",
       "length"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_REFERENCE_201703
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect a handful of genomic‑variant rows to confirm the join field
SELECT "reference_name",
       "variant_id",
       "start",
       "end"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count total variants in the genomic call‑set
SELECT COUNT(*)        AS "total_genomic_variants"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count total variants in the transcriptome call‑set
SELECT COUNT(*)        AS "total_transcriptome_variants"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_TRANSCRIPTOME_201703;
```

```sql
-- 5. Genomic variants per reference sequence
SELECT "reference_name",
       COUNT(*)        AS "genomic_variant_cnt"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703
GROUP  BY "reference_name"
ORDER  BY "genomic_variant_cnt" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Transcriptome variants per reference sequence
SELECT "reference_name",
       COUNT(*)        AS "transcript_variant_cnt"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_TRANSCRIPTOME_201703
GROUP  BY "reference_name"
ORDER  BY "transcript_variant_cnt" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine genomic & transcript counts per reference (inner join on reference_name)
WITH geno AS (
  SELECT "reference_name",
         COUNT(*) AS "geno_cnt"
  FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703
  GROUP  BY "reference_name"
),
tx AS (
  SELECT "reference_name",
         COUNT(*) AS "tx_cnt"
  FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_TRANSCRIPTOME_201703
  GROUP  BY "reference_name"
)
SELECT COALESCE(g."reference_name", t."reference_name") AS "reference_name",
       COALESCE(g."geno_cnt", 0)                        AS "geno_cnt",
       COALESCE(t."tx_cnt", 0)                          AS "tx_cnt",
       COALESCE(g."geno_cnt", 0) + COALESCE(t."tx_cnt",0) AS "total_variants"
FROM   geno g
FULL   JOIN tx t
ON     g."reference_name" = t."reference_name"
ORDER  BY "total_variants" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Join variant counts to the reference table and compute variant density (genomic only)
WITH var_cnt AS (
  SELECT "reference_name",
         COUNT(*) AS "variant_cnt"
  FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703
  GROUP  BY "reference_name"
)
SELECT r."name"                    AS "reference_sequence",
       r."length",
       v."variant_cnt",
       v."variant_cnt" / r."length"::FLOAT AS "variant_density"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_REFERENCE_201703 r
JOIN   var_cnt v
ON     r."name" = v."reference_name"
ORDER  BY "variant_density" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same as (8) but combining genomic + transcript variants
WITH geno AS (
  SELECT "reference_name",
         COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
  FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703
  GROUP  BY "reference_name"
),
tx AS (
  SELECT "reference_name",
         COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
  FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_TRANSCRIPTOME_201703
  GROUP  BY "reference_name"
),
tot AS (
  SELECT COALESCE(g."reference_name", t."reference_name") AS "reference_name",
         COALESCE(g."cnt",0) + COALESCE(t."cnt",0)        AS "total_cnt"
  FROM   geno g
  FULL   JOIN tx t
  ON     g."reference_name" = t."reference_name"
)
SELECT r."name"                                 AS "reference_sequence",
       r."length",
       t."total_cnt",
       t."total_cnt" / r."length"::FLOAT        AS "variant_density"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_REFERENCE_201703 r
JOIN   tot t
ON     r."name" = t."reference_name"
ORDER  BY "variant_density" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL QUERY: give the single reference sequence having the highest variant density
WITH geno AS (
  SELECT "reference_name",
         COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
  FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_201703
  GROUP  BY "reference_name"
),
tx AS (
  SELECT "reference_name",
         COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
  FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_TRANSCRIPTOME_201703
  GROUP  BY "reference_name"
),
tot AS (
  SELECT COALESCE(g."reference_name", t."reference_name") AS "reference_name",
         COALESCE(g."cnt",0) + COALESCE(t."cnt",0)        AS "total_cnt"
  FROM   geno g
  FULL   JOIN tx t
  ON     g."reference_name" = t."reference_name"
)
SELECT r."name"                                 AS "reference_sequence_with_highest_variant_density",
       r."length",
       t."total_cnt",
       t."total_cnt" / r."length"::FLOAT        AS "variant_density"
FROM   GENOMICS_CANNABIS.GENOMICS_CANNABIS.MNPR01_REFERENCE_201703 r
JOIN   tot t
ON     r."name" = t."reference_name"
ORDER  BY "variant_density" DESC
LIMIT  1;
```

